WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
Our goal is to ensure that addressing the water crisis 

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:08.759
becomes an integral part of global environmental strategy.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.959
We have gathered at a time when the world

00:00:17.959 --> 00:00:19.560
is experiencing an unprecedented

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.720
global crisis in its development model.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.720
The water crisis is an integral part

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.720
of the general crisis and,

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:32.439
above all, the crisis of world politics.

00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:36.519
The problem is exacerbated by climate change.

00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:40.400
Access to water is becoming 

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.159
a source of international conflicts.

00:00:44.959 --> 00:00:48.439
80% of infectious diseases are caused

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:54.639
by the use of poor-quality water.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.360
In developing countries, 

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.800
about 95% of all surface water is polluted.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.720
In the European Union, 37 children die every day

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.639
from water-related diseases. 

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.639
Unfortunately, the policy response

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.879
has been slow in the face

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:17.879
of this emergency.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.720
If it continues, tomorrow it will be too late.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:26.319
I believe that all of us, including Europe,

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.519
are responsible for the current situation.

00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:32.079
Europe deserves credit:

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:35.000
during a difficult decade, 

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.800
it has taken the lead

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.039
in the efforts to develop

00:01:40.039 --> 00:01:44.280
a new global environmental agenda.

00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:46.680
We should formalise the idea that water,

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:50.360
as the most important human resource,

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.519
is common property

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:54.639
and access to it

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.079
should be proclaimed

00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:59.759
a fundamental human right.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.280
I hope that our discussion will become a contribution

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:10.720
to the current research on which,

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.319
without exaggeration,

00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:15.680
the future of mankind will depend.

00:02:15.839 --> 00:02:16.800
Thank you for your attention.

